  "name": "summit-tor",
  "notes": "A tor is granite that rotted inward along its joints while it was still buried, until only rounded cores were left, and then had the rotten rock stripped off it. The stack of boulders still sitting on the old fracture grid is the tell, and it is what says the tor GREW here rather than being dropped here. It was previously one lumpy pyramid with a note claiming it was a stack of blocks. Two settings decide whether it reads: block_size_m 3.2 makes the cores BOULDER-sized rather than a lattice of small ones (at 2.6 it came out as a wall of eggs), and corestone is held at 0.46 - at 0.52 it reads as a better stack and then sheds two thirds of itself, because the boulders stop touching and a build now ships one connected piece. angular is down to 0.30 so the joint-aligned facets stop squaring off the outside of the pile. A landmark you navigate by, so it is authored rare and widely spaced.",
